[FINAL-TEXT] === DIAGNOSIS ===
is_anomaly: false
faulty_devices: none
diagnosis_text:
I cannot reproduce any isolation of the “other rack” or loss of its uplinks. End-to-end connectivity between hosts is healthy: from pc_0_0 (10.0.0.2) to pc_0_1 (10.0.1.2) we see 0% packet loss over 10 ICMP probes with ~1–2 ms RTT, and the reverse direction is equally clean. The fabric control-plane and links in that rack are up. On leaf_router_0_1 (top-of-rack for pc_0_1), both uplinks eth0 and eth1 report Link detected: yes, and the corresponding spine interfaces (spine_router_0_0:eth2 and spine_router_0_1:eth2) also show link up. BGP on leaf_router_0_1 has both spine neighbors (172.16.0.6 and 172.16.0.10) Established, exchanging prefixes; its routing table contains a BGP-learned route to 10.0.0.0/24 via 172.16.0.6. Conversely, leaf_router_0_0 has a BGP route to 10.0.1.0/24 via 172.16.0.8. These observations are exactly the opposite of what we would see if both uplinks were down (no BGP adjacencies and no remote-subnet routes).

Root cause: No fault found; the reported outage is not present and is not reproducible with current evidence.

Corrective fix: None required. The fabric is operating normally. If the issue recurs, please capture timestamps and a short packet/ARP trace on the affected host to isolate any transient or host-specific condition. We will continue to monitor. 
=== END ===